WEBVTT

00:00:09.762 --> 00:00:11.139
[yelling]

00:00:25.027 --> 00:00:27.196
This is amazing!

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:29.240
No longer amazing!

00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:30.658
Toothless!

00:00:30.741 --> 00:00:32.076
[shrieks]

00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:34.328
Oh, no!

00:00:35.663 --> 00:00:37.373
[screams]

00:00:39.959 --> 00:00:42.378
[Hiccup grunting] Whoa!

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.882
[sighs]

00:00:52.388 --> 00:00:53.389
Whoo!

00:00:54.098 --> 00:00:56.392
That really came out of nowhere.

00:01:00.605 --> 00:01:02.106
[Toothless groaning]

00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:06.068
We got to work on your
solo gliding there, bud.

00:01:06.235 --> 00:01:07.653
That locked-up tail

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.199
makes for some pretty sloppy
rescue maneuvers, hey?

00:01:27.673 --> 00:01:28.966
Ah!

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:31.385
Looks like we found another one, bud.

00:01:31.761 --> 00:01:32.929
[grumbles]

00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:34.680
Oh!

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:38.518
Oh, what, do you want an apology?

00:01:38.726 --> 00:01:41.771
Is that why you're pouting, big baby boo?

00:01:41.854 --> 00:01:43.314
[grumbling]

00:01:43.397 --> 00:01:44.774
Well, try this on! [grunts]

00:01:45.566 --> 00:01:47.777
Oh, you feeling it yet? Huh?

00:01:47.944 --> 00:01:51.155
Picking up on all of my
heartfelt remorse? [grunting]

00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:54.575
Oh, come on, come on.

00:01:54.742 --> 00:01:57.453
You wouldn't hurt a one-legged… [screams]

00:01:59.121 --> 00:02:02.208
You're right! You're right!
You win. You win.

00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:04.377
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa! [laughs]

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.379
He's down. And it's ugly.

00:02:06.546 --> 00:02:09.382
Dragons and Vikings, enemies again,

00:02:09.549 --> 00:02:12.593
locked in combat to the bitter… Oh!

00:02:16.472 --> 00:02:17.890
[groans]

00:02:19.475 --> 00:02:21.269
You know that doesn't wash out.

00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:23.145
[laughs]

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.421
So, what should we name it?

00:02:49.297 --> 00:02:51.257
"Itchy Armpit" it is.

00:02:52.675 --> 00:02:53.968
What do you reckon, bud?

00:02:54.135 --> 00:02:57.305
Think we might find a few
Timberjacks in those woods?

00:02:57.471 --> 00:03:00.099
The odd Whispering Death
or two in the rocks?

00:03:01.142 --> 00:03:05.980
Who knows? Maybe we'll finally
track down another Night Fury.

00:03:07.481 --> 00:03:09.275
Wouldn't that be something?

00:03:10.109 --> 00:03:12.903
[sighs]
So, what do you say? Just keep going?

00:03:12.987 --> 00:03:14.572
[grumbles]

00:03:14.655 --> 00:03:15.906
[dragon screeching]

00:03:22.663 --> 00:03:24.290
Afternoon, milady.

00:03:24.707 --> 00:03:26.167
Where have you been?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.294
[chuckles] Hi.

00:03:28.794 --> 00:03:32.006
Oh, winning races, what else?

00:03:32.173 --> 00:03:33.799
The real question is,

00:03:33.966 --> 00:03:35.051
where have you been?

00:03:35.217 --> 00:03:36.469
Avoiding my dad.

00:03:36.594 --> 00:03:38.304
Oh, no. What happened now?

00:03:38.512 --> 00:03:40.556
Oh, you're gonna love this.

00:03:40.681 --> 00:03:42.892
I wake up. The sun is shining.

00:03:43.059 --> 00:03:45.728
Terrible Terrors
are singing on the rooftop.

00:03:45.895 --> 00:03:47.188
I saunter down to breakfast

00:03:47.355 --> 00:03:49.815
thinking all is right
with the world and I get,

00:03:50.107 --> 00:03:52.026
[imitating Stoick] "Son, we need to talk."

00:03:52.276 --> 00:03:54.320
[imitating Hiccup]
"Not now, Dad. I got a whole day

00:03:54.403 --> 00:03:56.447
"of goofing off
to get started." [snickers]

00:03:56.614 --> 00:03:59.325
Okay, first of all,
I don't sound like that.

00:03:59.492 --> 00:04:00.910
Who is this character?

00:04:01.035 --> 00:04:04.997
And second, what is that
thing you're doing with my shoulders?

00:04:05.122 --> 00:04:08.209
Yeah, that's a truly
flattering impersonation.

00:04:08.417 --> 00:04:10.127
Anyway, he goes,

00:04:10.711 --> 00:04:13.923
[imitating Stoick] "You're the pride
of Berk, son, and I couldn't be prouder."

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.591
[imitating Hiccup] "Aw, thanks, Dad."

00:04:15.758 --> 00:04:18.344
"I'm pretty impressed with myself, too."

00:04:18.594 --> 00:04:21.305
[laughing] When have I ever
done that with my hands?

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.015
You just did.

00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:26.811
Okay. Just hold still.

00:04:27.686 --> 00:04:29.438
-[chuckles]
-This is very serious.

00:04:31.774 --> 00:04:33.567
[imitating Stoick] "You're all grown up,

00:04:33.651 --> 00:04:36.445
"and since no chief
could ask for a better successor,

00:04:36.612 --> 00:04:37.613
"I've decided…"

00:04:37.696 --> 00:04:38.989
To make you chief!

00:04:39.156 --> 00:04:41.951
Oh, my gods! Hiccup, that's amazing!

00:04:42.034 --> 00:04:43.244
[grunts] Ow!

00:04:43.327 --> 00:04:45.287
You're gonna wear out the spring coil.

00:04:45.371 --> 00:04:47.415
The calibration is very sensitive.

00:04:47.498 --> 00:04:48.666
[dragons shrieking]

00:04:48.749 --> 00:04:49.875
[both grunting]

00:04:52.378 --> 00:04:53.963
Yeah, so…

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.383
this is what I'm dealing with.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.551
What did you tell him?

00:04:58.717 --> 00:05:02.388
I didn't. By the time
he turned around, I was gone.

00:05:02.471 --> 00:05:04.306
Huh, well,

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.392
it's a lot of responsibility.

00:05:06.559 --> 00:05:09.979
The map will have to wait for sure,

00:05:10.146 --> 00:05:11.480
and I'll need to fly Toothless,

00:05:11.564 --> 00:05:12.982
since you'll be too busy, but…

00:05:14.358 --> 00:05:15.401
[gasps]

00:05:16.569 --> 00:05:18.446
It's not me, Astrid.

00:05:18.779 --> 00:05:21.031
All those speeches and planning,

00:05:21.115 --> 00:05:23.451
and running the village, that's his thing.

00:05:23.576 --> 00:05:25.453
I think you're missing the point.

00:05:25.578 --> 00:05:28.497
I mean, "chief." What an honor.

00:05:28.622 --> 00:05:30.791
-I'd be pretty excited.
-I… [sighs]

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.127
I'm not like you.

00:05:33.294 --> 00:05:35.254
You know exactly who you are.

00:05:35.421 --> 00:05:37.214
You always have.

00:05:38.299 --> 00:05:39.884
But I'm still looking.

00:05:40.092 --> 00:05:42.428
I know that I'm not my father,

00:05:42.595 --> 00:05:45.514
and I never met my mother,

00:05:46.056 --> 00:05:47.850
so what does that make me?

00:05:53.314 --> 00:05:57.443
What you're searching for
isn't out there, Hiccup.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:59.403
It's in here.

00:06:00.488 --> 00:06:02.573
Maybe you just don't see it yet.

00:06:03.616 --> 00:06:05.075
-Ugh. Ugh!
-Maybe.

00:06:05.409 --> 00:06:07.119
But you know,

00:06:07.286 --> 00:06:09.747
there is something out there.

00:06:09.914 --> 00:06:11.665
Hiccup… [gasps]

